od’s execution."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"body"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The return value, if any, of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure parameter.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Often, the optimizer can eliminate bounds checks within an array","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm, but when that fails, invoking the same algorithm on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer pointer passed into your closure lets you trade safety for speed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example shows how modifying the contents of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UnsafeMutableBufferPointer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument to ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alters the contents of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the array:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","numbers.withUnsafeMutableBufferPointer { buffer in","    for i in stride(from: buffer.startIndex, to: buffer.endIndex - 1, by: 2) {","        buffer.swapAt(i, i + 1)","    }","}","print(numbers)","\/\/ Prints \"[2, 1, 4, 3, 5]\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The pointer passed as an argument to ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is valid only during the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"execution of ","type":"text"},{"code":"withUnsafeMutableBufferPointer(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Do not store or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"return the pointer for later use."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do not rely on anything about the array that is the target of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this method during execution of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" closure; it might not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"appear to have its correct value. Instead, use only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutableBufferPointer"},{"text":" argument to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning","style":"warning"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/UnsafeMutableBufferPointer":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/unsafemutablebufferpointer","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnsafeMutableBufferPointer"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A nonowning collection interface to a buffer of mutable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements stored contiguously in memory.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutableBufferPointer","title":"UnsafeMutableBufferPointer","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnsafeMutableBufferPointer"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/ArraySlice":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/arrayslice","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ArraySlice"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A slice of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContiguousArray"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArraySlice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ArraySlice","title":"ArraySlice","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"